  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Kim Beom-soo (Korean: 김범수; born March 8, 1966), also known as Brian Kim, is a South Korean billionaire businessman who is the founder and chairman of Kakao, a South Korean internet company. He is among the richest people in South Korea. As of August 2026, Forbes estimated his net worth as US$3.2 billion and ranked him 1,327th on its list of the world’s richest people.\n\n",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
